## Tables

`etable` renders models as `"gt"`, `"md"`, `"tex"`, `"typst"`, or `"df"`; see [Regression Tables](tutorials/regression-tables.qmd).

::: {#0a3501fb .cell execution_count=39}
``` {.python .cell-code}
fits = [pf.feols("Y ~ X1 + X2", data=data), pf.feols("Y ~ X1 + X2 | f1", data=data)]
pf.etable(fits, type="md", drop=["X2"])
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}
```
|                           | ('Y', '(1)')   | ('Y', '(2)')   |
|:--------------------------|:---------------|:---------------|
| ('coef', 'X1')            | -0.995***      | -0.950***      |
|                           |  (0.082)       |  (0.066)       |
| ('coef', 'Intercept')     | 0.890***       |                |
|                           |  (0.108)       |                |
| ('fe', 'f1')              | -              | x              |
| ('stats', 'Observations') | 997            | 997            |
| ('stats', 'R²')           | 0.177          | 0.489          |
```
:::
